{"component_id_namespace":"ec077a53-0b40-5f21-b1fe-a62094d2476b","component_schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","components":[{"attributes":{"code":"TMC","legacy_node_id":"ks-topeka:tmc:10.65.150","page_type":"section"},"citation":"10.65.150","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/10.65.150","content_hash":"e999fe8ebbe43530cdd01189d08cd86527df63bea10a048c127e06b2f71a977e","heading":"Share-a-ride program.","ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":null,"schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.65.150:section","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/10.65.150","text":"(a) As an alternative to all other rates of fare of taxicabs, a taxicab business may offer a share-a-ride program, the elements of which include the grouping of passengers and the cost per passenger determined on a per square mile basis. The share-a-ride program shall be optional to the passenger. The maximum rates of fare for conveying persons in the share-a-ride program shall be as follows:\n(1) | For the first square mile | $3.00\n(2) | For each succeeding square mile | $1.00\n(3) | For each person age 12 or over riding with the passenger | $0.25\n(1)\nFor the first square mile\n$3.00\n(2)\nFor each succeeding square mile\n$1.00\n(3)\nFor each person age 12 or over riding with the passenger\n$0.25\n(b) The rate of fare to the passenger shall be determined as if the trip was a straight line from point of origin to point of destination; however, a taxicab driver may deviate from the straight line trip and pick up and deliver additional passengers. (Code 1981 § 46-42.2. Code 1995 § 154-122.)","type":"section","workbench_component_id":"aa2bccdf-0f2d-587d-bc84-106cd8260cad"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"10.65.150","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/10.65.150","content_hash":"e5cece097a136e01e315c4af899658b5b5e123cbdd7cce7afb3505e3360c0937","heading":null,"ordinal":0,"parent_source_comp